I’m adding here the [*link*|https://docs.google.com/document/d/15l6Xug7dFJBqeQCr7E8UQoH9A4CFdM3O/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=104915744464167918221&rtpof=true&sd=true] to the updated Agreement.

Also, here are the comments from the supplier on the main questions raised in the previous version:
*1.1 Definitions*

*c) Business day:* At Bolt we don't account Saturdays as business days, can you please elaborate on this point and the potential liabilities for us? {color:#0747a6}_We have taken this into consideration and amended the agreement accordingly. Business day shall be Monday to Friday._{color}

*g) Personal information:* Was changed to Personal Data, and we added more info. Accepted

# Provision of the bulk SMS Service

*2.2* We included an initial term of 1 Year + Automatic renewal for another year, please let us know if this works for you: {color:#0747a6}_Agreed_{color}

# Parties' obligations

*4.1 The Client's obligations*

*4.1.4* We need clarification on which Authorities, type of penalties and if they can be challenged.

{color:#0747a6}_the authority referred to here is the Communication Authority of Kenya (CA). It is the regulating authority for telecommunication service providers in Kenya. The penalties for breach CA regulations are in form of fines. The said penalties can also be challenged if wrongfully imposed._{color}

*4.1.6, c)* Can you please confirm if there is a national spamming opt-out list in Kenya {color:#0747a6}_Yes, there is a universal USSD CODE that is *456*9*5# for customers who wish to opt-out._{color}

*4.1.8* Can you please provide full visibility on this regulation, and also how we can keep ourselves updated in case there are any changes: {color:#0747a6}_the regulations are available on CA website. For full visibility on the reulations use the link_ {color}[https://www.ca.go.ke/sector-regulations|https://www.ca.go.ke/sector-regulations|smart-link] 

{color:#0747a6}_In case of change of regulations the authority notifys the public through its website._    {color}

*4.1.10* Bolt will only be responsible for indemnifying Advanta if the breach is directly attributed to Bolt's gross negligence or willful misconduct. {color:#0747a6}_Agreed_{color}

*4.2 Advanta's obligations*

Addition of *4.2.5-11,* also we added *quality metrics and penalties* in case of non-compliance (attributable to the Supplier's service) {color:#0747a6}_Agreed_{color}

# Remuneration

*5.2* NET5 is too small for our local ops to process the invoices, our corporate standard is NET15, can you please review if this works for you? {color:#0747a6}_Agreed_{color}

# Availability and interruption of the service

Addition of *Service Availability, Service Outage* and *quality metrics -* {color:#0747a6}*_Agreed_*{color}

# Support Services

{color:#0747a6}_We are proposing escalation channels such as Slack, ticketing platform or email Use this 2 emails:__  {color}[{color:#0747a6}_Info@advantasms.com_{color}|mailto:Info@advantasms.com]{color:#0747a6} _and_ {color}[{color:#0747a6}_Lisper.muthoni@advantasms.com_{color}|mailto:Lisper.muthoni@advantasms.com]

Addition of Clause *10. Data Protection*

*12. Termination*

*12.2, b)* The amounts owed must be reviewed and agreed by both parties, and we need to include a dispute time for it. {color:#0747a6}_We propose 30 days period for dispute time._{color}

Please let me know if you need additional information.

Thanks and regards

