the problem can be in the {{MarkdownConverter}} class, {{getCustomMarkdownRenderer}} function [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/platform/beehive/beehive_cms/main/service/MarkdownConverter.ts#L18-L37|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/platform/beehive/beehive_cms/main/service/MarkdownConverter.ts#L18-L37]
I suggest refactoring {{convertToHtml}} function to this: 

{noformat}public convertToHtml(markdown: string, directory: string): string {
    marked.use({
        renderer: {
            table: (header: string, body: string): string {
                return new marked.Renderer()
                    .table(header, body)
                    .replace("<table", `<table border="1" ${MarkdownConverter.TABLE_BORDER_STYLES_ATTR}`);
            },
            image: (href: string, title: string, text: string): string {
                const imageLink = MarkdownConverter.isUrl(href)
                    ? href
                    : this.imageUrlGenerator.generateImageLinkReplacement(path.join(directory, href));
                return new marked.Renderer()
                    .image(imageLink, title, text)
                    .replace("<img", '<img style="max-width: 100%;"');
            },
        }
    });

    return marked.parse(markdown).trim();
}{noformat}

Or the problem can be in the use of the {{marked}} library as it is used today.

