Hey David,

According to the tax team, the following info should be disclosed in the invoices:
+Business with VAT registration+ - 
- the invoice number and the date of issue; 
*- the name and surname (title), address, personal identification number or VAT identification number of the supplier;* 
- the name and surname (title), address, personal identification number or VAT identification number of the customer; - the nature and extent of the services rendered; 
- the date on which the supply of goods or services was made if it differs from the date of issue of invoice; 
- the unit price exclusive of VAT or the consideration for goods or services supplied, categorized by VAT rates; 
- discounts or rebates if they are not included in the unit price; 
- the VAT rate; 
- the VAT amount payable, categorized by VAT rates;
 - the total amount of the consideration and the VAT amount.


So, we can only specify the info about the supplier, i.e., fleet.

No, it’s not exactly like this.

Case 1- is for bad photos. Here we have unlimited ability to retry. There is no account suspension involved at all. However the driver can still not go online. They can just try the selfie again and again, until they pass.

Case 2- fraud cases - this is where suspension takes place. There is no investigation; they are blocked right away. Meaning there is an infinite blocking of their account. We actually updated the language on this screen and we are in process of changing it to:

{quote}We couldn't verify your identity. Your account will be blocked. You may appeal the suspension by contacting Bolt.{quote}

(we are waiting on translations, right now it says

