Hey [~accountid:610a3ee66051c5006aeeeea1], In relation to your question, below see below my understanding of the situation:

* The TVDE law determines the following information obligations to electronic platforms:
** 17(4) - For the purposes of the licensing referred to in paragraph 1, the interested party must submit the following information elements the following information:
a) Company name;
b) Tax identification number;
c) Head office;
d) Name or brands adopted for operation;
e) Electronic address;
f) Holders of the administrative, management or management and respective criminal record certificates;
g) Articles of association;
h) Entries in public registers and respective registration numbers registration numbers.
** 17(5) - In addition to the elements referred to in the preceding paragraph, t*he operator who operates electronic platforms and who does not head office in Portugal must notify IMT, I. P., of a representative in national territory* identified through the presentation of the elements referred to in the previous article.
** 17(8) - *The information referred to in paragraphs 4 and 5 shall be available on the electronic platform for consultation by any interested party*, with the exception of the indication of holders of the administrative, management or management bodies and the memorandum and articles of association.
* Given these obligations it appears to me that the reference to the representative is essential. I understand that the local PT entity is the representative in Portugal of Bolt Operations.
* Therefore, it appears to me that in the t&c of TVDE operators and Passengers we would need to make reference to the local entity. On the contrary, I do not see a reason to keep a reference to the local entity in the taxi t&c, since the TVDE law is not applicable in this case. I’ve included this reference in the review tracker.
* Since 1/1/2023 the rentals business is localised and therefore the t&c should refer the PT entity only.

Thank you and please let me know if you have any further questions.

